{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "09Y8", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-pullback-locally-constant}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a96be3aec28592c979c1bd6e5a1ed8fa4c4ccc67558c33f1691f32e2dae2f5d3", "source_text": "Holds for any morphism of topoi, see\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a9b978962ccacd76a9c8c9aa696a2253120c61a29b4056c6194a05e360232e3b", "unit_id": "tag:095A:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "09Y8", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Lambda$", "MATH_0004": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0005": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$Y_\\etale$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-pushforward-locally-constant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e0dc68256f4a524e1b68a3a1e3405466b94bef37118aea6fcc482ff9bf8375a8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3978f3a324bc88ae7ee5a27bda37f05c70078f28d818355e93d7f4c0a410010c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a finite <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism of schemes.\nIf <MATH_0002> is a (finite) locally constant sheaf of sets,\n(finite) locally constant sheaf of abelian groups, or\n(finite type) locally constant sheaf of <MATH_0003>-modules\non <MATH_0004>, the same is true for <MATH_0005>\non <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8fd461538352a5f6147fce01cf33d0e20da17da4da1fb9b3848236daeec39d96", "unit_id": "tag:095B:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "09Y8", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'E", "MATH_0001": "$f_*$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}_i$", "MATH_0003": "$i = 1, \\ldots, n$", "MATH_0004": "$\\prod_{i = 1, \\ldots, n} \\mathcal{F}_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{etale-lemma-finite-etale-etale-local}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5cf771c23c77bad3d50ce9a01fc4840d8ddff44e321005bfd24f0ec30f576c62", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d40e646752b5ebb3e2c832011632d249268daac56a1151a3642fe5918461d8ff", "source_text": "The construction of <MATH_0001> commutes with <ACCENT_0001>tale localization.\nA finite <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism is locally isomorphic to a disjoint union\nof isomorphisms, see\n<ACCENT_0003>tale Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThus the lemma says that if <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003>\nare (finite) locally constant sheaves of sets, then\n<MATH_0004> is too.\nThis is clear. Similarly for sheaves of abelian groups and modules.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e6c09c07b66c728d1c3e3b73ca2de9e3544a8b3c7b605a98a4061daf1747964e", "unit_id": "tag:095B:proof"}
